WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.302 --> 00:00:03.024
- There's no such thing to
me as an embarrassing moment.

00:00:03.024 --> 00:00:04.220
No such thing.

00:00:04.220 --> 00:00:06.350
If I tripped and fell,
if my bra strap showed,

00:00:06.350 --> 00:00:09.334
if my slip fell off, if
I fell flat on my face,

00:00:09.334 --> 00:00:11.368
there's no such thing as
an embarrassing moment.

00:00:11.368 --> 00:00:12.823
When you think about what it means

00:00:12.823 --> 00:00:14.850
to be a human being on the
planet Earth right now,

00:00:14.850 --> 00:00:16.791
that's pretty awesome.

00:00:16.791 --> 00:00:19.640
Money's worth nothing if it can't buy you

00:00:19.640 --> 00:00:21.659
the opportunity to love more.

00:00:21.659 --> 00:00:23.607
- She's best known for her talk show,

00:00:23.607 --> 00:00:26.813
which was the highest rated
TV program of its kind.

00:00:26.813 --> 00:00:28.187
Several assessments rank her

00:00:28.187 --> 00:00:31.083
as the most influential
woman in the world.

00:00:31.083 --> 00:00:33.820
She's been ranked as the
richest African American

00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:35.133
of the 20th century.

00:00:35.133 --> 00:00:36.811
She's Oprah Winfrey, and here's my take

00:00:36.811 --> 00:00:39.931
on her top 10 rules for
success, volume two.

00:00:39.931 --> 00:00:41.985
Rule number five is my personal favorite

00:00:41.985 --> 00:00:44.415
and I'm curious to know which
one you guys like the best.

00:00:44.415 --> 00:00:46.212
And as always, guys, as
you're watching the videos,

00:00:46.212 --> 00:00:48.484
if you hear something that
really resonates with you,

00:00:48.484 --> 00:00:50.539
please leave it down in the comments below

00:00:50.539 --> 00:00:52.219
and put quotes around it so other people

00:00:52.219 --> 00:00:53.512
can be inspired as well.

00:00:53.512 --> 00:00:55.375
Also, as you are writing something down,

00:00:55.375 --> 00:00:58.226
it's much more likely to
stick in your head, too.

00:00:58.226 --> 00:00:59.059
Enjoy.

00:01:00.236 --> 00:01:03.379
(whooshing and banging)

00:01:03.379 --> 00:01:06.296
(triumphant music)

00:01:11.565 --> 00:01:12.659
(whooshing)

00:01:12.659 --> 00:01:15.084
- I think that success is a process

00:01:15.084 --> 00:01:18.501
and I believe that my first Easter speech

00:01:20.051 --> 00:01:22.143
in the Kosciusko Baptist Church

00:01:22.143 --> 00:01:25.351
at the age of 3 1/2 was the beginning

00:01:25.351 --> 00:01:29.620
and that every other speech,
every other book I read,

00:01:29.620 --> 00:01:34.602
every other time I spoke in
public was a building block

00:01:34.602 --> 00:01:38.442
so that by the time I
first sat down to audition

00:01:38.442 --> 00:01:41.440
in front of a television camera
and somebody says read this,

00:01:41.440 --> 00:01:43.758
what allowed me to read it so comfortably

00:01:43.758 --> 00:01:46.449
and be so at ease with myself at that time

00:01:46.449 --> 00:01:48.278
was the fact that I'd
been doing it awhile.

00:01:48.278 --> 00:01:50.040
If I'd never read a
book or I'd never spoken

00:01:50.040 --> 00:01:53.220
in public before, I would
have been traumatized by it.

00:01:53.220 --> 00:01:56.840
So the fact that we went on the air

00:01:56.840 --> 00:02:01.338
with the Oprah Winfrey
Show in 1986, nationally,

00:02:01.338 --> 00:02:04.307
and people'd say, oh,
but you're so comfortable

00:02:04.307 --> 00:02:06.013
in front of the camera,
you can be yourself,

00:02:06.013 --> 00:02:09.559
well it's because I've been
being myself since I was 19.

00:02:09.559 --> 00:02:11.588
And I would not have, I
would not have been able

00:02:11.588 --> 00:02:13.567
to be as comfortable with myself

00:02:13.567 --> 00:02:17.100
had I not made mistakes on the air

00:02:17.100 --> 00:02:20.257
and been allowed to
make mistakes on the air

00:02:20.257 --> 00:02:23.466
and understand that it doesn't matter.

00:02:23.466 --> 00:02:25.311
You know, I, there's no such thing to me

00:02:25.311 --> 00:02:26.312
as an embarrassing moment.

00:02:26.312 --> 00:02:27.522
No such thing.

00:02:27.522 --> 00:02:30.073
If I tripped and fell,
if my bra strap showed,

00:02:30.073 --> 00:02:32.855
if my slip fell off, if
I fell flat on my face,

00:02:32.855 --> 00:02:34.888
there's no such thing as
an embarrassing moment

00:02:34.888 --> 00:02:37.324
because I know that there's not a moment

00:02:37.324 --> 00:02:40.512
that I could possibly
experience on the air

00:02:40.512 --> 00:02:42.623
that somebody hasn't already experienced.

00:02:42.623 --> 00:02:46.751
So when it happens, you
say, oh, my slip fell off!

00:02:46.751 --> 00:02:48.461
And it's no big deal.

00:02:48.461 --> 00:02:50.284
I mean, like, I was on TV the other day

00:02:50.284 --> 00:02:52.510
and somebody says oh,
Oprah, you have a run.

00:02:52.510 --> 00:02:54.745
Have you not seen a run
before in your life?

00:02:54.745 --> 00:02:56.934
Well I get them, too, let me tell you.

00:02:56.934 --> 00:03:00.037
So I mean, yeah, I can't be embarrassed.

00:03:00.037 --> 00:03:01.037
I can't be embarrassed.

00:03:01.037 --> 00:03:02.850
Now, when I first started out,

00:03:02.850 --> 00:03:06.391
that was not true because I was under the,

00:03:06.391 --> 00:03:08.295
I was pretending to be somebody I was not.

00:03:08.295 --> 00:03:09.903
I was pretending to be Barbara Walters.

00:03:09.903 --> 00:03:11.162
So I'd go to a news conference

00:03:11.162 --> 00:03:15.361
and I was more interested in
how I phrased the question.

00:03:15.361 --> 00:03:18.262
And how eloquent the question sounded,

00:03:18.262 --> 00:03:20.035
as opposed to listening to the answer.

00:03:20.035 --> 00:03:21.908
I was so, which always happens

00:03:21.908 --> 00:03:23.871
when you're interested
in impressing people

00:03:23.871 --> 00:03:25.406
instead of doing what
you're supposed to be doing.

00:03:25.406 --> 00:03:26.960
And it took me awhile.

00:03:26.960 --> 00:03:31.127
It took me messing up on the
air on, during a live newscast.

00:03:32.186 --> 00:03:33.996
I was doing a list of foreign countries

00:03:33.996 --> 00:03:35.960
and I, there was all these foreign names

00:03:35.960 --> 00:03:39.502
and then Canada was thrown in
and I called Canada Ku-na-dah.

00:03:39.502 --> 00:03:41.845
And I got so tickled that I called Canada,

00:03:41.845 --> 00:03:44.529
I go, that wasn't
Ku-na-dah, that was Canada.

00:03:44.529 --> 00:03:47.216
Excuse me, that wasn't
Canada, that wasn't Ku-na-dah,

00:03:47.216 --> 00:03:48.424
that was Canada.

00:03:48.424 --> 00:03:50.074
And then I started laughing.

00:03:50.074 --> 00:03:54.184
Well, it was, it became the
first real moment I ever had.

00:03:54.184 --> 00:03:56.629
And the news director later said to me

00:03:56.629 --> 00:03:58.398
well if you do that then
you should just keep going,

00:03:58.398 --> 00:04:00.154
you shouldn't correct
yourself and let people know.

00:04:00.154 --> 00:04:02.043
Well I know, well who's
ever heard of Ku-na-dah?

00:04:02.043 --> 00:04:05.971
So that was for me the
beginning of realizing that

00:04:05.971 --> 00:04:09.557
oh, you can laugh at yourself
and you can make a mistake

00:04:09.557 --> 00:04:11.005
and it's not the end of the world.

00:04:11.005 --> 00:04:13.667
You don't have to be perfect.

00:04:13.667 --> 00:04:15.251
Biggest lesson for me for television

00:04:15.251 --> 00:04:17.676
because then it didn't matter.

00:04:17.676 --> 00:04:19.829
Didn't matter, oh, sorry,
bra strap's showing.

00:04:19.829 --> 00:04:24.215
What inspired me was
and is, continues to be,

00:04:24.215 --> 00:04:27.730
what continues to inspire me is a

00:04:27.730 --> 00:04:30.147
primal and fundamental desire

00:04:31.241 --> 00:04:33.991
to fulfill the highest expression

00:04:35.949 --> 00:04:38.416
of myself as a human being.

00:04:38.416 --> 00:04:40.249
I don't want to die...

00:04:42.237 --> 00:04:44.820
Not having completely burnt out

00:04:47.211 --> 00:04:50.544
every single possibility of my humanity.

00:04:52.146 --> 00:04:55.491
I just, I just want to,
when I leave this planet,

00:04:55.491 --> 00:04:58.183
I want everybody to say you did that,

00:04:58.183 --> 00:05:00.651
used it all up, not
another thing I could do.

00:05:00.651 --> 00:05:02.823
There wasn't another
person I could have given

00:05:02.823 --> 00:05:06.590
of myself to, there wasn't
another deed I could have done.

00:05:06.590 --> 00:05:07.725
- Sure.
- There wasn't another,

00:05:07.725 --> 00:05:09.191
that you just want to, you want to say

00:05:09.191 --> 00:05:11.573
I want to fill it up!

00:05:11.573 --> 00:05:14.408
You want to take this
whole human existence,

00:05:14.408 --> 00:05:15.868
which, when you think about it, Godfrey,

00:05:15.868 --> 00:05:17.944
is really pretty damn miraculous.

00:05:17.944 --> 00:05:18.777
- [Godfrey] It is.

00:05:18.777 --> 00:05:19.610
- It is.
- It is.

00:05:19.610 --> 00:05:20.707
- When you think about what it means

00:05:20.707 --> 00:05:23.008
to be a human being on the
planet Earth right now,

00:05:23.008 --> 00:05:25.485
that's pretty awesome.

00:05:25.485 --> 00:05:28.838
So I just want to, I want
to take that to the max.

00:05:28.838 --> 00:05:32.809
I want to say no need
to come back as a human.

00:05:32.809 --> 00:05:34.026
Angel status.

00:05:34.026 --> 00:05:35.274
- I know you hate this phrase,

00:05:35.274 --> 00:05:38.903
but what is your brand, do you think?

00:05:38.903 --> 00:05:40.095
- I'm the love brand.

00:05:40.095 --> 00:05:41.827
(Piers laughs)

00:05:41.827 --> 00:05:42.992
- Aren't we all, darling?

00:05:42.992 --> 00:05:44.826
- No, I'm the love brand.
- Aren't we all?

00:05:44.826 --> 00:05:46.591
- Oh, I'm the love brand.

00:05:46.591 --> 00:05:48.449
- You like to shower love around?

00:05:48.449 --> 00:05:51.792
- Yeah, it's really, that's
what it is, I'm the love

00:05:51.792 --> 00:05:52.783
- Love that!
- And connection brand.

00:05:52.783 --> 00:05:54.241
That's what I am.

00:05:54.241 --> 00:05:55.531
- You're a bit like Barry
White was the love god,

00:05:55.531 --> 00:05:56.837
you're the love brand.

00:05:56.837 --> 00:05:57.836
- I'm the love brand.

00:05:57.836 --> 00:06:00.903
'Cause ultimately,
everything that I'm saying,

00:06:00.903 --> 00:06:02.136
whether it's in my magazine,

00:06:02.136 --> 00:06:04.450
whether it's Gayle on the radio

00:06:04.450 --> 00:06:07.466
or whether it's the Oprah Winfrey Show

00:06:07.466 --> 00:06:10.245
and now everything about the channel OWN,

00:06:10.245 --> 00:06:14.808
it's about opening your
space, your heart space,

00:06:14.808 --> 00:06:16.071
so that you can love more.

00:06:16.071 --> 00:06:18.317
You know, that's really all money is for.

00:06:18.317 --> 00:06:20.317
Money's worth nothing if it can't buy you

00:06:20.317 --> 00:06:22.734
the opportunity to love more.

00:06:23.708 --> 00:06:25.338
You can't call in sick.

00:06:25.338 --> 00:06:28.671
You can't ever give less than 100%.

00:06:29.979 --> 00:06:32.237
And if you are sick, which I
have been a couple of times,

00:06:32.237 --> 00:06:35.484
that's when you got to pull up to 110, 120

00:06:35.484 --> 00:06:38.650
because people have come
from all over the country

00:06:38.650 --> 00:06:39.894
and this is their moment.

00:06:39.894 --> 00:06:41.184
They've saved their money, they've bought

00:06:41.184 --> 00:06:42.691
the airline tickets, they got new outfits,

00:06:42.691 --> 00:06:45.293
they called their sisters,
their cousins, their aunts,

00:06:45.293 --> 00:06:46.986
their mother-in-laws, their mothers,

00:06:46.986 --> 00:06:50.177
and that is why they're there, to see you.

00:06:50.177 --> 00:06:54.344
So I feel a sense of responsibility,
a sense of obligation,

00:06:55.224 --> 00:06:58.899
a sense of respect, reverence,
honor for those people.

00:06:58.899 --> 00:07:02.428
First day I went to school,
I was in a classroom.

00:07:02.428 --> 00:07:06.232
By the time I was, you
know, six years old,

00:07:06.232 --> 00:07:07.775
didn't go to school
until I was six years old

00:07:07.775 --> 00:07:08.909
'cause I was living with my
grandmother at that time.

00:07:08.909 --> 00:07:09.742
- [Godfrey] Sure.

00:07:09.742 --> 00:07:10.910
- But she had taught me how to read,

00:07:10.910 --> 00:07:12.181
read the Bible, Bible stories.

00:07:12.181 --> 00:07:16.928
So I went into the
classroom knowing Nicodemus,

00:07:16.928 --> 00:07:19.080
Shadrach, Meshach, and Abednego.

00:07:19.080 --> 00:07:21.283
I could spell all of those words.

00:07:21.283 --> 00:07:23.929
I thought I was, you know,
I was preaching to the,

00:07:23.929 --> 00:07:25.445
to my kindergarten teacher.
- You learnt all that?

00:07:25.445 --> 00:07:28.896
- (laughs) So she's like who is this girl?

00:07:28.896 --> 00:07:32.482
So I was never placed in an environment

00:07:32.482 --> 00:07:35.845
where I was ever made to feel inferior.

00:07:35.845 --> 00:07:38.469
I always felt like I'm the
smartest kid in this room.

00:07:38.469 --> 00:07:41.724
And because I was never placed in a,

00:07:41.724 --> 00:07:45.837
never put in a position where
I was made to feel less than,

00:07:45.837 --> 00:07:48.055
I didn't grow up feeling
less than, you know?

00:07:48.055 --> 00:07:50.033
- Right, and the rest,
as they say, is history.

00:07:50.033 --> 00:07:51.577
- And the rest is history.
- 'Cause we know from there--

00:07:51.577 --> 00:07:53.598
- And it's all about what
you believe, you know?

00:07:53.598 --> 00:07:57.751
I say this to, and I do
something on my network now

00:07:57.751 --> 00:08:02.456
called Life Class, the
fundamental key to success

00:08:02.456 --> 00:08:06.342
is what you believe is true for yourself,

00:08:06.342 --> 00:08:09.210
not what you want, not what you desire.

00:08:09.210 --> 00:08:11.092
It's what do you believe, you know?

00:08:11.092 --> 00:08:12.259
You could say I wanted,

00:08:12.259 --> 00:08:13.863
I want to be the most
successful person in the world,

00:08:13.863 --> 00:08:15.958
but if you believe that
there's a glass ceiling

00:08:15.958 --> 00:08:17.184
and you're going to have a hard time

00:08:17.184 --> 00:08:18.639
kicking through that glass ceiling--

00:08:18.639 --> 00:08:19.639
- You'll keep yourself down--
- You will be defined

00:08:19.639 --> 00:08:21.480
by the glass ceiling.

00:08:21.480 --> 00:08:24.549
And the great beauty and gift of my life

00:08:24.549 --> 00:08:27.737
is that I was never defined by the box

00:08:27.737 --> 00:08:29.885
that other people tried to put me in.

00:08:29.885 --> 00:08:33.474
Fame comes with the mission and purpose.

00:08:33.474 --> 00:08:37.641
You know, you cannot define
me or try to put me in a box

00:08:40.234 --> 00:08:42.579
and you can't look at my life unless

00:08:42.579 --> 00:08:44.845
you look at the whole life.

00:08:44.845 --> 00:08:47.012
So I am a negro, formerly.

00:08:49.294 --> 00:08:51.544
Born in 1954 in Mississippi

00:08:53.287 --> 00:08:56.704
at a time when it was an apartheid state.

00:08:58.317 --> 00:09:00.900
And to be sitting here with you

00:09:02.077 --> 00:09:05.410
as your first guest in 2011 is a miracle

00:09:06.811 --> 00:09:11.675
that is beyond anything I
could actually do for myself.

00:09:11.675 --> 00:09:14.400
So there's something greater at work here.

00:09:14.400 --> 00:09:18.024
And the thing that's greater at work,

00:09:18.024 --> 00:09:20.631
the force that has, enforces,

00:09:20.631 --> 00:09:23.020
that have made this happen in my life,

00:09:23.020 --> 00:09:26.353
along with me working as hard as I have,

00:09:27.648 --> 00:09:32.217
is it's bigger than I am
and fame is the vehicle

00:09:32.217 --> 00:09:35.378
from which I get to have this platform.

00:09:35.378 --> 00:09:36.878
So do I like that?

00:09:38.002 --> 00:09:39.880
I appreciate it.

00:09:39.880 --> 00:09:42.600
If I had been what I
thought I was going to be

00:09:42.600 --> 00:09:45.888
and that is a great fourth grade teacher,

00:09:45.888 --> 00:09:48.015
I would have also liked that

00:09:48.015 --> 00:09:51.505
because at the core of me, I am a teacher

00:09:51.505 --> 00:09:55.309
and I am happiest when
I feel that people are

00:09:55.309 --> 00:09:57.299
getting something, learning something,

00:09:57.299 --> 00:09:59.376
enhancing themselves in a way

00:09:59.376 --> 00:10:01.543
that they'd never thought of before.

00:10:01.543 --> 00:10:02.880
And that's really truly one of my

00:10:02.880 --> 00:10:06.606
favorite moments on television
or in any experience,

00:10:06.606 --> 00:10:09.117
when I'm just one on one with a friend

00:10:09.117 --> 00:10:11.061
or somebody I don't even know,

00:10:11.061 --> 00:10:12.428
being able to share something with them

00:10:12.428 --> 00:10:14.974
and they think I never thought of it, gee!

00:10:14.974 --> 00:10:17.263
Stedman and I were in a hotel

00:10:17.263 --> 00:10:19.822
watching some bad television

00:10:19.822 --> 00:10:23.873
and I was complaining about
the state of television,

00:10:23.873 --> 00:10:25.398
talk shows in particular.

00:10:25.398 --> 00:10:26.916
And he said why don't you change it?

00:10:26.916 --> 00:10:28.483
Why don't you just get your own network?

00:10:28.483 --> 00:10:31.815
And I thought that that
was a ridiculous idea.

00:10:31.815 --> 00:10:33.300
And then he started to talk about it

00:10:33.300 --> 00:10:34.799
and he wrote some things down

00:10:34.799 --> 00:10:38.427
and I saw the word OWN, and I thought OWN,

00:10:38.427 --> 00:10:41.816
O-W, oh, that's my, those are my initials.

00:10:41.816 --> 00:10:43.535
And I said wouldn't it be something

00:10:43.535 --> 00:10:45.874
if I could create a network
that was really about

00:10:45.874 --> 00:10:50.129
mindful, and I underlined
the word mindful, television.

00:10:50.129 --> 00:10:52.219
- [Barbara] 15 years
later, those scribblings

00:10:52.219 --> 00:10:54.994
came closer to reality
when she was approached

00:10:54.994 --> 00:10:58.424
by David Zaslav, the president
of the Discovery Network.

00:10:58.424 --> 00:11:01.021
- My view was if we want to do
this, you have to be all in.

00:11:01.021 --> 00:11:05.188
She paused and then she said
to me, "It's meant to be."

00:11:06.863 --> 00:11:10.194
And we shook hands and
that's how our journey began.

00:11:10.194 --> 00:11:12.212
- At first I thought oh great, a network,

00:11:12.212 --> 00:11:13.607
oh gee, this is the dream I had, oh,

00:11:13.607 --> 00:11:15.844
and I actually showed
him the piece of paper

00:11:15.844 --> 00:11:17.301
where I'd written it
down and Stedman said,

00:11:17.301 --> 00:11:21.270
and as that started to settle in with me,

00:11:21.270 --> 00:11:25.544
I thought whoa, what is this
I've gotten myself into?

00:11:25.544 --> 00:11:28.506
This is a lot more work
than I ever imagined.

00:11:28.506 --> 00:11:29.507
- Are you scared?

00:11:29.507 --> 00:11:30.509
- Very scared.

00:11:30.509 --> 00:11:32.330
I was very scared.

00:11:32.330 --> 00:11:34.319
And I would wake up in
the middle of the night,

00:11:34.319 --> 00:11:37.382
literally (gasps) like clutching my chest.

00:11:37.382 --> 00:11:38.768
Like what have I done?

00:11:38.768 --> 00:11:40.642
What have I done?

00:11:40.642 --> 00:11:42.397
- What if you fail?

00:11:42.397 --> 00:11:44.438
- That's what I was afraid of.

00:11:44.438 --> 00:11:45.599
That's what I was afraid of.

00:11:45.599 --> 00:11:49.525
The reason why I made the
decision to go forward

00:11:49.525 --> 00:11:51.192
is because I believe

00:11:53.130 --> 00:11:55.380
that people deserve to have

00:11:56.638 --> 00:12:00.860
value-centered inspirational
programming for themselves.

00:12:00.860 --> 00:12:05.027
I believe that television
has become, in many ways...

00:12:06.354 --> 00:12:08.271
Banal, it has become...

00:12:10.940 --> 00:12:12.416
Insipid.

00:12:12.416 --> 00:12:15.263
And not every, not all of it,

00:12:15.263 --> 00:12:17.507
but I think that I have
something to offer.

00:12:17.507 --> 00:12:21.077
I did this at the end of my show.

00:12:21.077 --> 00:12:23.614
I did my favorite guest of all time,

00:12:23.614 --> 00:12:26.557
and that's hard to do out of literally

00:12:26.557 --> 00:12:29.230
thousands and thousands.
(Godfrey mumbles)

00:12:29.230 --> 00:12:30.685
They supposedly estimated
that there's like

00:12:30.685 --> 00:12:33.613
35,000 people I interviewed
over the years, but...

00:12:33.613 --> 00:12:36.615
There was one woman, out
of all the celebrities,

00:12:36.615 --> 00:12:38.282
out of all of the...

00:12:39.525 --> 00:12:41.490
Famous, non-famous, infamous people.

00:12:41.490 --> 00:12:43.687
One woman--
- Who was she?

00:12:43.687 --> 00:12:44.974
- Who was she?

00:12:44.974 --> 00:12:47.609
Her name is Tererai Trent.

00:12:47.609 --> 00:12:49.794
Listen to this story.

00:12:49.794 --> 00:12:52.040
I'm going to try to shorten
it for you, Godfrey.

00:12:52.040 --> 00:12:53.151
- Please do, please do.

00:12:53.151 --> 00:12:54.949
- Okay, Tererai Trent, born and raised

00:12:54.949 --> 00:12:56.633
in a village in Zimbabwe.

00:12:56.633 --> 00:12:59.339
11 years old, she's doing
her brother's homework.

00:12:59.339 --> 00:13:01.357
She wants to go to school,
her father says no,

00:13:01.357 --> 00:13:02.749
- 'Cause you have to--
- You're a girl.

00:13:02.749 --> 00:13:03.898
- [Godfrey] You have to
educate the boy first.

00:13:03.898 --> 00:13:04.999
- Yep, that's right.
- That was the tradition.

00:13:04.999 --> 00:13:06.841
- That's right, the boy
has to go to school.

00:13:06.841 --> 00:13:08.098
You can't go to school.

00:13:08.098 --> 00:13:10.117
So she starts doing
her brother's homework.

00:13:10.117 --> 00:13:12.537
She does her brother's
homework, he goes to school.

00:13:12.537 --> 00:13:14.401
He gets all As on his homework

00:13:14.401 --> 00:13:15.960
yet he doesn't know the
answer to the question.

00:13:15.960 --> 00:13:17.478
The teacher comes to the village to say

00:13:17.478 --> 00:13:18.881
what is going on here?

00:13:18.881 --> 00:13:22.022
This boy doesn't know the answer
but his homework's perfect.

00:13:22.022 --> 00:13:24.978
She finds out that Tererai,
his younger sister,

00:13:24.978 --> 00:13:25.838
is doing his homework.

00:13:25.838 --> 00:13:28.489
She begs the father to
let Tererai go to school.

00:13:28.489 --> 00:13:30.856
The father says no,
she can't go to school.

00:13:30.856 --> 00:13:32.897
Finally, he marries her off.

00:13:32.897 --> 00:13:35.178
She marries at 11 1/2 years old.

00:13:35.178 --> 00:13:36.744
She gets married.

00:13:36.744 --> 00:13:40.399
She has three children by
the time she's 18 years old.

00:13:40.399 --> 00:13:43.415
A woman comes to the village from an NGO,

00:13:43.415 --> 00:13:46.597
Heifer International, and
asks what are your dreams.

00:13:46.597 --> 00:13:47.734
This is going to make me cry.

00:13:47.734 --> 00:13:49.301
Finally you're going to make me cry!

00:13:49.301 --> 00:13:50.134
- [Godfrey] (laughs) Got it.

00:13:50.134 --> 00:13:51.898
- Asks her what are your dreams?

00:13:51.898 --> 00:13:54.952
This child has never thought
about what her dreams were.

00:13:54.952 --> 00:13:56.302
She says write down your dreams.

00:13:56.302 --> 00:13:58.443
She writes down her
dreams on a piece of paper

00:13:58.443 --> 00:13:59.929
and she folds 'em in a tin can

00:13:59.929 --> 00:14:02.085
and she buries them under a rock.

00:14:02.085 --> 00:14:05.236
The first dream was to
be able to go to a school

00:14:05.236 --> 00:14:09.316
in the United States of America
and get a college degree.

00:14:09.316 --> 00:14:13.066
She ends up, through
some miracle of the NGO,

00:14:14.022 --> 00:14:16.294
going to the United States.
- Wow.

00:14:16.294 --> 00:14:18.779
- She gets a college degree.

00:14:18.779 --> 00:14:19.979
- Wow.
- Yeah.

00:14:19.979 --> 00:14:21.836
She gets a four year
degree in three years.

00:14:21.836 --> 00:14:23.133
Tererai Trent.

00:14:23.133 --> 00:14:25.949
She goes back to the rock in Zimbabwe.

00:14:25.949 --> 00:14:29.248
She writes her next goal
on the piece of paper.

00:14:29.248 --> 00:14:30.777
She buries it under the rock,

00:14:30.777 --> 00:14:34.087
she writes I want to get a masters degree.

00:14:34.087 --> 00:14:36.059
She goes back to the United States,

00:14:36.059 --> 00:14:37.606
she gets a masters degree!

00:14:37.606 --> 00:14:39.588
By this time, she now has five children.

00:14:39.588 --> 00:14:41.546
She's married to a man
who still beats her.

00:14:41.546 --> 00:14:43.070
- Oh, incredible.
- Incredible.

00:14:43.070 --> 00:14:44.406
She goes back to the United States.

00:14:44.406 --> 00:14:45.441
She gets her masters degree.

00:14:45.441 --> 00:14:46.578
After the masters degree,

00:14:46.578 --> 00:14:49.470
she goes back to the rock in Zimbabwe.

00:14:49.470 --> 00:14:51.336
She writes down her final goal

00:14:51.336 --> 00:14:52.650
is to get a doctorate degree.

00:14:52.650 --> 00:14:56.317
And last year, she
became Dr. Tererai Trent.

00:14:57.368 --> 00:14:58.351
- Where did you find it?

00:14:58.351 --> 00:15:00.867
- Where did I find it?

00:15:00.867 --> 00:15:04.867
I found her in Nicholas
Kristof's book called...

00:15:07.337 --> 00:15:10.230
Something the sky, underneath
the sky or the sky.

00:15:10.230 --> 00:15:12.306
I found her in Nicholas Kristof's book.

00:15:12.306 --> 00:15:13.139
- [Godfrey] Incredible.

00:15:13.139 --> 00:15:14.086
- Mm-hmm.
- Incredible.

00:15:14.086 --> 00:15:15.800
- And I was reading the story.

00:15:15.800 --> 00:15:17.645
I had Nicholas Kristof on the show,

00:15:17.645 --> 00:15:20.861
Nicholas Kristof, the famous
New York Times writer.

00:15:20.861 --> 00:15:22.611
And she wasn't there.

00:15:23.757 --> 00:15:25.057
She wasn't a part of the show.

00:15:25.057 --> 00:15:26.898
I'm reading this story, I
can't believe this book,

00:15:26.898 --> 00:15:28.943
this story of this woman,
as I'm reading the story.

00:15:28.943 --> 00:15:31.303
So when we go to do the show,

00:15:31.303 --> 00:15:33.347
the producers have Nicholas Kristof on.

00:15:33.347 --> 00:15:36.330
They bring on other guests
but this woman isn't there.

00:15:36.330 --> 00:15:37.794
I go how could you not have her there?

00:15:37.794 --> 00:15:41.474
So we tape another show
with Nicholas Kristof,

00:15:41.474 --> 00:15:42.901
we go back, I go find,

00:15:42.901 --> 00:15:45.539
we're going to find that
woman, Tererai Trent.

00:15:45.539 --> 00:15:46.538
And this time,

00:15:46.538 --> 00:15:47.703
by this time she's living
in the United States.

00:15:47.703 --> 00:15:51.881
We followed her back to
Zimbabwe to the rock.

00:15:51.881 --> 00:15:55.730
We pulled the tin can
from underneath the rock.

00:15:55.730 --> 00:15:57.971
And that is my favorite guest of all time.

00:15:57.971 --> 00:16:00.373
- [Godfrey] And the worst?

00:16:00.373 --> 00:16:01.206
- I don't have a worst.

00:16:01.206 --> 00:16:02.242
I don't have a worst.

00:16:02.242 --> 00:16:05.020
But the reason why she, and
as I said this on my show,

00:16:05.020 --> 00:16:08.271
the reason why Tererai
Trent is my favorite guest

00:16:08.271 --> 00:16:12.836
of all time is because she
represents, in that one story

00:16:12.836 --> 00:16:15.453
of the little girl in
a village in Zimbabwe

00:16:15.453 --> 00:16:18.703
who had a dream and the heart and depth

00:16:19.674 --> 00:16:21.527
and discipline to pursue it.

00:16:21.527 --> 00:16:24.260
She represents everything I tried to say

00:16:24.260 --> 00:16:26.891
in every show in 25 years.

00:16:26.891 --> 00:16:28.721
She literally, through her life story,

00:16:28.721 --> 00:16:31.460
sums up the message that I was trying

00:16:31.460 --> 00:16:33.957
to give to every single one of my viewers.

00:16:33.957 --> 00:16:35.374
You can, you can.

00:16:36.439 --> 00:16:37.487
Keep trying.

00:16:37.487 --> 00:16:39.051
Don't give up.

00:16:39.051 --> 00:16:40.053
- [Godfrey] You have to believe.

00:16:40.053 --> 00:16:41.057
- You have to believe.

00:16:41.057 --> 00:16:43.651
The thing that I do best, Piers,

00:16:43.651 --> 00:16:45.305
you didn't ask me that question.

00:16:45.305 --> 00:16:46.915
Oprah, what is it you do best?

00:16:46.915 --> 00:16:50.616
- (clears throat) Oprah, what
is it you do best? (laughs)

00:16:50.616 --> 00:16:54.783
- The thing that I strive to
do best is be here, be now.

00:16:56.266 --> 00:16:58.619
Right here, right now, with you.

00:16:58.619 --> 00:16:59.988
The reason why we've had such a good time

00:16:59.988 --> 00:17:03.216
is 'cause I'm not thinking
about if somebody else is.

00:17:03.216 --> 00:17:05.251
But I'm not thinking about
how much time do we have left

00:17:05.251 --> 00:17:06.516
and how many questions
you 're going to have

00:17:06.516 --> 00:17:07.521
and what are you going to ask me.

00:17:07.521 --> 00:17:09.839
Just be here, be now.

00:17:09.839 --> 00:17:12.887
So that I can enjoy this experience.

00:17:12.887 --> 00:17:15.304
And so I don't have a lot of,

00:17:16.695 --> 00:17:18.274
I don't live in the past.

00:17:18.274 --> 00:17:20.805
I don't carry the past into this moment

00:17:20.805 --> 00:17:22.210
'cause I do the Oprah Show.

00:17:22.210 --> 00:17:23.341
I learned how not to do that.

00:17:23.341 --> 00:17:24.876
That's what all of those years

00:17:24.876 --> 00:17:27.675
of non-therapy but paying attention

00:17:27.675 --> 00:17:28.880
to the guests on the show,

00:17:28.880 --> 00:17:30.148
the way they live their lives,

00:17:30.148 --> 00:17:32.535
what the experts had to
say, what I've learned

00:17:32.535 --> 00:17:34.515
from paying attention.

00:17:34.515 --> 00:17:36.718
- Have you ever seen her before?

00:17:36.718 --> 00:17:37.873
- [Oprah] We've been
driving for a long time.

00:17:37.873 --> 00:17:39.554
- [Gayle] Does she look
like Oprah Winfrey to you?

00:17:39.554 --> 00:17:40.387
- She does.
- Yes.

00:17:40.387 --> 00:17:41.852
- [Gayle] That's her.

00:17:41.852 --> 00:17:44.320
(laughter)

00:17:44.320 --> 00:17:46.436
- No, you're not.

00:17:46.436 --> 00:17:48.487
(laughter)

00:17:48.487 --> 00:17:50.238
- [Gayle] She doesn't look like herself?

00:17:50.238 --> 00:17:51.263
- Yeah.

00:17:51.263 --> 00:17:52.377
- But you really are?

00:17:52.377 --> 00:17:53.893
- Really.

00:17:53.893 --> 00:17:55.572
Staying in the tipi.

00:17:55.572 --> 00:17:56.573
Tipi one.

00:17:56.573 --> 00:17:58.063
- But don't tell anyone we're here.

00:17:58.063 --> 00:17:59.647
(laughter)

00:17:59.647 --> 00:18:00.745
- Okay, what's the ZIP code for me?

00:18:00.745 --> 00:18:02.853
- Oh my!
- 60606.

00:18:02.853 --> 00:18:04.816
- I'm Oprah!
- I know you are, honey.

00:18:04.816 --> 00:18:06.101
But you really are you.

00:18:06.101 --> 00:18:08.020
- I'm really Oprah, I
really am, I really am.

00:18:08.020 --> 00:18:09.388
- No, you're not.

00:18:09.388 --> 00:18:10.885
- Yes, I am, I am!

00:18:10.885 --> 00:18:13.368
(women scream)

00:18:13.368 --> 00:18:14.439
- You be the penis.

00:18:14.439 --> 00:18:15.536
- Yeah.
- All right.

00:18:15.536 --> 00:18:16.988
(laughter)
It's limp, it's limp.

00:18:16.988 --> 00:18:19.182
- Nobody has ever said
that to me in my life.

00:18:19.182 --> 00:18:21.476
(laughter)

00:18:21.476 --> 00:18:25.290
I have been talking to
people my whole life

00:18:25.290 --> 00:18:28.684
and nobody has ever
said, "You be the penis."

00:18:28.684 --> 00:18:30.958
This is a letter I wrote to Anthony Otey.

00:18:30.958 --> 00:18:32.513
(laughter)

00:18:32.513 --> 00:18:33.521
I was such a geek.

00:18:33.521 --> 00:18:34.984
(laughter)

00:18:34.984 --> 00:18:37.984
It says, "On today, June 22nd, 1971,

00:18:39.014 --> 00:18:41.950
"I've decided to voice
my thoughts on paper

00:18:41.950 --> 00:18:45.255
"to prevent my brain
from becoming disrupted."

00:18:45.255 --> 00:18:47.360
- Oh my god.
(laughter)

00:18:47.360 --> 00:18:50.229
Voice my thoughts on paper?

00:18:50.229 --> 00:18:52.479
(laughter)

00:18:53.674 --> 00:18:55.200
That was in high school?

00:18:55.200 --> 00:18:58.206
- That was in high
school, June 22nd, okay.

00:18:58.206 --> 00:18:59.630
(clears throat) Today--

00:18:59.630 --> 00:19:01.796
- She's always been very
dramatic, don't you think?

00:19:01.796 --> 00:19:03.782
- "Today is my ninth
anniversary with Anthony.

00:19:03.782 --> 00:19:05.900
"Nine months today.

00:19:05.900 --> 00:19:07.112
"Never thought I'd make it this far.

00:19:07.112 --> 00:19:08.235
(laughter)

00:19:08.235 --> 00:19:09.791
"My father says," oh, there we were.

00:19:09.791 --> 00:19:11.165
(laughter)

00:19:11.165 --> 00:19:12.543
There's me with the flip.

00:19:12.543 --> 00:19:14.746
That was the Marlo Thomas That Girl flip.

00:19:14.746 --> 00:19:17.755
"My father says stay at home and rest.

00:19:17.755 --> 00:19:19.745
"Doesn't he know that love knows no rest?"

00:19:19.745 --> 00:19:21.995
(laughter)

00:19:24.888 --> 00:19:26.875
- [Gayle] Nice vest, Anthony.

00:19:26.875 --> 00:19:30.753
- "That for those who love, time is not.

00:19:30.753 --> 00:19:33.672
"I love Anthony, I really,
truly, truly love him"--

00:19:33.672 --> 00:19:34.753
- [Gayle] Truly, truly, truly.

00:19:34.753 --> 00:19:36.405
- "And I don't give a blank."

00:19:36.405 --> 00:19:38.580
I used the blanks in case my
father ever found the letters.

00:19:38.580 --> 00:19:40.005
I wouldn't be cursing.

00:19:40.005 --> 00:19:42.116
"Whether or not people think it's proper

00:19:42.116 --> 00:19:44.816
"or whether I'm too
aggressive or flipped for him

00:19:44.816 --> 00:19:46.849
"because I don't think God will mind.

00:19:46.849 --> 00:19:47.835
(laughter)

00:19:47.835 --> 00:19:49.578
"There's so much hatred in the world,

00:19:49.578 --> 00:19:51.445
"I should think God would be happy to see

00:19:51.445 --> 00:19:52.983
"a little love flowing
every now and then."

00:19:52.983 --> 00:19:55.233
(laughter)

00:19:56.186 --> 00:19:57.932
- Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:19:57.932 --> 00:20:00.577
I hope you enjoyed this
volume two edition.

00:20:00.577 --> 00:20:02.477
If you liked it, you
might want to check out

00:20:02.477 --> 00:20:03.361
volume one as well.

00:20:03.361 --> 00:20:04.745
It was pretty spectacular.

00:20:04.745 --> 00:20:06.279
I'd also love to know what did Oprah say

00:20:06.279 --> 00:20:08.226
that had the biggest
impact on you and why?

00:20:08.226 --> 00:20:09.609
What are you going to take from this video

00:20:09.609 --> 00:20:12.023
and immediately apply to your
life or to your business?

00:20:12.023 --> 00:20:13.693
Leave it down in the comments below

00:20:13.693 --> 00:20:14.817
and I'll see what I can do.

00:20:14.817 --> 00:20:16.700
I also want to give a quick
shout out to Maria Pasca.

00:20:16.700 --> 00:20:18.659
Thank you so much for
picking up a copy of my book,

00:20:18.659 --> 00:20:21.786
Your One Word, and for
making that really fun

00:20:21.786 --> 00:20:24.346
and interesting promo picture for it.

00:20:24.346 --> 00:20:26.570
I really appreciate the
love that you put into it.

00:20:26.570 --> 00:20:27.809
Thank you guys again for watching.

00:20:27.809 --> 00:20:29.092
I believe in you.

00:20:29.092 --> 00:20:30.875
I hope you continue to
believe in yourself.

00:20:30.875 --> 00:20:33.857
And whatever your one word is, much love.

00:20:33.857 --> 00:20:35.168
I'll see you soon.

00:20:35.168 --> 00:20:38.501
(whooshing and banging)

00:20:41.212 --> 00:20:43.549
- This is what people don't know.

00:20:43.549 --> 00:20:44.565
'Cause you can't tell everybody.

00:20:44.565 --> 00:20:47.148
I am who I am, one black woman,

00:20:48.866 --> 00:20:52.396
my hand in God's hand,
trusting in that word

00:20:52.396 --> 00:20:55.243
'cause that word never failed me.

00:20:55.243 --> 00:20:58.826
And I got to where I
am and I stand as I am

00:20:59.942 --> 00:21:02.175
as Maya Angelou often says,

00:21:02.175 --> 00:21:06.249
and often said, and says in
her poem, too, Our Grandmothers

00:21:06.249 --> 00:21:09.249
every time you see me, I come as one

00:21:10.196 --> 00:21:12.567
but I stand as 10,000.

00:21:12.567 --> 00:21:14.097
(crowd cheers)

00:21:14.097 --> 00:21:16.204
Every time you see me.

00:21:16.204 --> 00:21:19.837
I come as one but I stand as 10,000.

00:21:19.837 --> 00:21:21.611
So it's just not me standing up here,

00:21:21.611 --> 00:21:25.122
it's every, it's my
mother, my grandmother,

00:21:25.122 --> 00:21:26.900
her mother, the mother before her,

00:21:26.900 --> 00:21:29.829
her grandfather, every uncle who prayed.

00:21:29.829 --> 00:21:31.976
Every sister who cried.

00:21:31.976 --> 00:21:34.246
Every aunt who sacrificed.

00:21:34.246 --> 00:21:37.587
Those whose names made the history books,

00:21:37.587 --> 00:21:40.906
those whose names never
could make the history books

00:21:40.906 --> 00:21:45.073
who allowed me to come as
one and stand as 10,000.

00:21:46.096 --> 00:21:47.341
(applause)

00:21:47.341 --> 00:21:49.747
So oftentimes when I walk into a room

00:21:49.747 --> 00:21:51.343
just as cool as you please

00:21:51.343 --> 00:21:54.919
and I can't see another black
face in a 50-mile radius,

00:21:54.919 --> 00:21:56.545
(laughter)

00:21:56.545 --> 00:21:59.545
I stand and sit at the boards as one

00:22:00.917 --> 00:22:03.843
but I'm bringing the 10,000 behind me.

00:22:03.843 --> 00:22:04.844
(crowd cheers)

00:22:04.844 --> 00:22:07.729
Because I not only know who I am

00:22:07.729 --> 00:22:09.979
but I also know Whose I am.

00:22:11.112 --> 00:22:13.906
(crowd cheers)

00:22:13.906 --> 00:22:16.656
And so anything you hear about me

00:22:17.557 --> 00:22:20.359
that feels good, sounds
good, you think about.

00:22:20.359 --> 00:22:21.490
I wonder what Oprah's doing.

00:22:21.490 --> 00:22:22.487
How's she doing?

00:22:22.487 --> 00:22:24.035
I am living the dream.

00:22:24.035 --> 00:22:26.026
(crowd cheers)

00:22:26.026 --> 00:22:28.731
And I want you to live the dream.

00:22:28.731 --> 00:22:31.979
Because I'm not living the
dream because I'm special.

00:22:31.979 --> 00:22:34.718
I'm living the dream
because I was obedient

00:22:34.718 --> 00:22:37.254
to the call of the dream.

00:22:37.254 --> 00:22:39.837
(crowd cheers)

00:22:40.686 --> 00:22:43.504
So I want you to leave here today

00:22:43.504 --> 00:22:46.921
thinking about what is the dream for you.

00:22:48.789 --> 00:22:51.510
What is God's dream for you?

00:22:51.510 --> 00:22:54.930
What does the Creator's
dream hold for you?

00:22:54.930 --> 00:22:58.384
So often, we spend our
lives wishing and hoping

00:22:58.384 --> 00:23:00.916
and hoping and wishing
and desiring things.

00:23:00.916 --> 00:23:03.497
This is what I know for sure.

00:23:03.497 --> 00:23:05.683
You don't get what you wish for.

00:23:05.683 --> 00:23:07.030
You don't even get what you hope for.

00:23:07.030 --> 00:23:08.643
You get what you believe.

00:23:08.643 --> 00:23:10.493
(crowd cheers)

00:23:10.493 --> 00:23:12.576
So what is it you believe

00:23:13.475 --> 00:23:16.392
and know to be God's dream for you?

00:23:17.836 --> 00:23:19.372
So I'm living the dream.

00:23:19.372 --> 00:23:21.316
I'm living in the space of the dream.

00:23:21.316 --> 00:23:22.910
And the dream's good, dream's good.

00:23:22.910 --> 00:23:24.562
(crowd cheers)

00:23:24.562 --> 00:23:25.918
The dream is greater than anything

00:23:25.918 --> 00:23:27.393
that I could have imagined.

00:23:27.393 --> 00:23:29.381
You know, when I was a little girl,

00:23:29.381 --> 00:23:32.830
my father, on Sunday
mornings, after church,

00:23:32.830 --> 00:23:35.410
he was a deacon so he
thought he had to say goodbye

00:23:35.410 --> 00:23:36.414
to every single person.

00:23:36.414 --> 00:23:38.566
We were the last car
leaving the parking lot

00:23:38.566 --> 00:23:40.048
in the green Oldsmobile.

00:23:40.048 --> 00:23:44.119
And we would drive through the
white people's neighborhood.

00:23:44.119 --> 00:23:45.519
And I used to dream the dream,

00:23:45.519 --> 00:23:47.310
driving through the white
people's neighborhood.

00:23:47.310 --> 00:23:49.308
We'd drive through the
white people's neighborhoods

00:23:49.308 --> 00:23:51.479
and you'd see their fancy houses.

00:23:51.479 --> 00:23:52.644
Some of 'em had gates.

00:23:52.644 --> 00:23:55.292
But all of 'em had trees.

00:23:55.292 --> 00:23:59.249
And I remember when I
first came to Baltimore,

00:23:59.249 --> 00:24:01.541
(crowd cheers)
I met a friend...

00:24:01.541 --> 00:24:02.979
Hello, Baltimore in the house!

00:24:02.979 --> 00:24:04.983
(crowd cheers)

00:24:04.983 --> 00:24:06.503
When I first came to Baltimore,

00:24:06.503 --> 00:24:08.527
I made friends with a wonderful woman

00:24:08.527 --> 00:24:10.114
named Arlene Weiner.

00:24:10.114 --> 00:24:12.265
She was the wealthiest
person I'd ever met.

00:24:12.265 --> 00:24:15.192
And I went to her house
and parked in the driveway

00:24:15.192 --> 00:24:18.003
there was a Corvette and there was a BMW

00:24:18.003 --> 00:24:19.207
and there as a Mercedes.

00:24:19.207 --> 00:24:21.457
I went whoa, Arlene's rich.

00:24:23.173 --> 00:24:27.071
And at Arlene's house, once I got inside,

00:24:27.071 --> 00:24:30.216
I could see from her kitchen window

00:24:30.216 --> 00:24:33.211
six trees in the front yard.

00:24:33.211 --> 00:24:35.096
I thought oh rich people have trees.

00:24:35.096 --> 00:24:36.428
(laughter)

00:24:36.428 --> 00:24:38.648
When I get rich, I'm going
to get me some trees.

00:24:38.648 --> 00:24:39.878
I'm not just going to get me,

00:24:39.878 --> 00:24:42.626
everybody want to get cars
and pocketbooks and shoes.

00:24:42.626 --> 00:24:44.709
But I want me some trees.

00:24:45.720 --> 00:24:47.803
So as life would have it,

00:24:48.825 --> 00:24:51.780
I was standing in my kitchen window

00:24:51.780 --> 00:24:54.829
about three years ago in California,

00:24:54.829 --> 00:24:56.553
making coffee in the morning.

00:24:56.553 --> 00:24:58.133
And I was looking out the window

00:24:58.133 --> 00:25:00.133
and I saw the six trees.

00:25:03.338 --> 00:25:04.611
(crowd cheers)

00:25:04.611 --> 00:25:05.776
But listen to me.

00:25:05.776 --> 00:25:07.899
I was making, making, making the coffee.

00:25:07.899 --> 00:25:09.478
I saw the six trees.

00:25:09.478 --> 00:25:11.478
I went out on the porch.

00:25:12.508 --> 00:25:15.251
To actually count the six trees.

00:25:15.251 --> 00:25:17.501
And this is what I noticed.

00:25:18.339 --> 00:25:20.589
That I could dream the six.

00:25:21.865 --> 00:25:26.121
But beyond the six trees
in my kitchen window,

00:25:26.121 --> 00:25:27.371
are 3687 trees.

00:25:31.128 --> 00:25:32.146
How do I know?

00:25:32.146 --> 00:25:33.460
'Cause I had 'em counted.

00:25:33.460 --> 00:25:37.377
(audience applauds and laughs)

00:25:38.484 --> 00:25:40.447
I had 'em counted.

00:25:40.447 --> 00:25:42.465
'Cause I said I want to know
how many trees out there.

00:25:42.465 --> 00:25:43.965
I dreamed the six.

00:25:45.267 --> 00:25:49.918
That's as much as my small
mind and my imagination

00:25:49.918 --> 00:25:52.067
could hold for myself.

00:25:52.067 --> 00:25:54.110
I dreamed the six

00:25:54.110 --> 00:25:56.596
but God can see beyond the six.

00:25:56.596 --> 00:25:59.179
(crowd cheers)

00:26:00.669 --> 00:26:03.037
Can see beyond the six

00:26:03.037 --> 00:26:06.370
because there was a bigger dream for me.

00:26:07.364 --> 00:26:09.141
And I'm here to tell you,

00:26:09.141 --> 00:26:13.335
there is a bigger dream for you, Essence.

00:26:13.335 --> 00:26:14.803
There's a bigger dream.

00:26:14.803 --> 00:26:17.886
And so the key, the secret, the magic

00:26:19.247 --> 00:26:22.497
is to surrender to God's dream for you.

00:26:24.687 --> 00:26:26.423
(crowd cheers)

00:26:26.423 --> 00:26:29.302
To quit fighting against
and pushing against

00:26:29.302 --> 00:26:33.593
and disallowing against
and resisting against

00:26:33.593 --> 00:26:38.099
and trying to tell the
Creator, the Universal Forces,

00:26:38.099 --> 00:26:41.432
Divine Intelligence what
you are supposed to do

00:26:41.432 --> 00:26:44.015
and get still and know for sure

00:26:47.098 --> 00:26:50.265
what His dream, The Dream is for you.

